{"step_index":1097,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:31:06Z","content":"### Why AI Texts Were Getting Cut Off & Errant\n\n1. **Artificial Token Truncation:**\n   - The generation configuration had `maxOutputTokens: 180` set. When Gemini generated conversational phrasing, punctuation, or internal reasoning tokens, it would hit that threshold and cut off mid-thought.\n2. **Missing Handwritten Note Prioritization:**\n   - The previous prompt didn't explicitly instruct the AI to highlight handwritten questions/notes on the report card.\n3. **Rigid Length Clamping:**\n   - The prompt had conflicting constraints forcing dense information into a restrictive character window.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Corrected\n\n1. **Expanded Token Headroom & Natural Completion ([`aiSmsService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/aiSmsService.ts)):**\n   - Increased `maxOutputTokens` to **`600`**, ensuring every generated text completes smoothly and ends with a clear closing question.\n   - Set prompt rules requiring complete sentences and prohibiting truncation.\n\n2. **Targeted Handwritten Note & Question Recognition:**\n   - The AI now scans for teacher handwritten questions (`custom_questions`) and notes (`lead.notes`).\n   - If a teacher wrote a note on their card, the message acknowledges it (e.g. *\"I have your FRS Report Card from Mainland High and saw your note asking about '...' and wanted to make sure we review your exact numbers.\"*).\n\n3. **Multi-Topic Focus Quick Chips ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx) & [`LeadDetailScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx)):**\n   - Added a **`📝 Address Note`** focus chip whenever the teacher has handwritten notes or custom questions.\n   - Quick chips for **`🎯 Meeting Slot`**, **`💰 5% Bonus & DROP`**, and **`🏫 Planning Period`** allow 1-tap tone adjustments.\n\n4. **Context-Aware Offline Fallback Engine:**\n   - If the API key is not yet configured or there is no network connection, the offline generator builds personalized SMS copy that includes the educator's handwritten note, planning period, classroom/room number, and service years.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Production Status\nThe updated build has been compiled and deployed live:\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**"}
